//Adding React through CDN
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html   lang="en">
    <title>
        Leraning React
    </title>
    <body>        
        <div id="root"></div>
        <script crossorigin src="https://unpkg.com/react@18/umd/react.development.js"></script>
        <script crossorigin src="https://unpkg.com/react-dom@18/umd/react-dom.development.js"></script>
        <script>      
            const rootEle =  document.getElementById("root");
            const element = React.createElement(
                "h1",
                {
                  className:"header-element",
                  id:"child"
                },
                "Hi,My name is Rohan"
            )
            const root = ReactDOM.createRoot(rootEle);
            root.render(element);
        </script>
    </body>
</html>

//Addinng react through npm
1. mkdir react-app
2. Inside react-app,run npm init -y.This add the package.json to the project
3. Run npm install react react-dom. This will add react and react-dom as dependencies to the project and also add the files to node_modules
4  npm install --save-dev webpack webpack-cli
5. Webpack need to know where to start from i.e. entry point for this create a file webpack.config.js in the root dir
6 Inside webpack-config.js add 
const path = require("path");

module.exports = {
    entry: "./src/main.js",
    output: {
        path: path.resolve(__dirname, "dist"),
        filename: "main.js"
    }
};
//This tells webpack to start from main.js and put the bundled code inside dist folder
7 npx webpack
This add the bundled file under dist folder
Notes: Webpack is a JavaScript module bundler that analyzes the dependencies of an application, processes the modules, 
and bundles them into files that can be loaded by the browser.
8 Now we need to connect index.html to the bundled js file for this add
<script src="./dist/main.js"></script> in the index.html
index.html (Open in browser)
    ↓
<script src="./dist/main.js">
    ↓
Webpack bundle
    ↓
React + ReactDOM + our code
    ↓
document.getElementById("root")
    ↓
root.render(...)
    ↓
UI
//This will work but everytime we change the code, we need to run npx webpack and manually re-load the browser. To solve this we need 
we need build tools that provide development servers and watch mode.

9. npm install --save-dev @babel/core
npm install --save-dev @babel/preset-react // tells babel to compile react
npm install --save-dev babel-loader //used by webpack to provide code to babel
If we want to use JSX. Browsers dont understand JSX directly neither does webpack. For this we need a complier (commonly used Babel)
Babel is a JavaScript compiler/transpiler that transforms modern JavaScript and JSX 
into JavaScript that can be understood by the target environment.

10. Configure Babel
Create babel.config.json and add
{
  "presets": ["@babel/preset-react"] //tells babel to use react preset
}
11. Configure webpack to use babel
In webpack.config.js add
 module: {
        rules: [
            {
                test: /\.jsx?$/,
                exclude: /node_modules/,
                use: "babel-loader"
            }
        ]
    }


***We can avoid all this manual configuration and use build tools like Vite to do all this for us

npm create vite@latest my-app -- --template react




